<title>JAPAN: Japan Aug M2+CD money supply up 3.7 pct yr/yr -BOJ.</title>
<headline>Japan Aug M2+CD money supply up 3.7 pct yr/yr -BOJ.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-09-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan's broadly defined money supply average of M2 plus certificates of deposit (CDs) grew a preliminary 3.7 percent in August from a year earlier, the Bank of Japan (BOJ) said on Wednesday.  </p>
<p>A breakdown of money supply figures follows:</p>
<p>(Year-on-year percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     AUG PRELIM   JUL REVISED JUNE</p>
<p> Unadjusted M2 + CDs     +3.7	 +3.7	+ 3.8</p>
<p>    M1			+14.1	+14.3	+16.3</p>
<p>    CDs		     +40.5	+54.0	+68.8</p>
<p>			     AUG PRELIM   JUL REVISED JUNE</p>
<p> Broadest money measure  +3.7	 +4.0	+ 4.2</p>
<p>(Annualised month-on-month percentage changes)</p>
<p>			     AUG PRELIM   JUL REVISED JUNE</p>
<p> Adjusted M2 + CDs	 +2.1	 -1.4	+ 8.8</p>
<p>(Average outstanding yen levels)</p>
<p>			   AUG PRELIM  JUL REVISED   JUNE</p>
<p>Unadjusted M2+CDs  556.8 trln  558.0 trln 555.2 trln</p>
<p>    M1		  163.7 trln  165.3 trln 163.3 trln</p>
<p>    CDs		  13.1 trln   12.8 trln  14.8 trln</p>
<p>			   AUG PRELIM  JUL REVISED  JUNE</p>
<p>Broadest liquidity 1,120.1 trln1,122.3 trln1,116.4 trln</p>
